\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Correct-attribution rate against problem size. Each approximate configuration is lightly smoothed (Gaussian filter, $\sigma =1$) with its raw per-size points overlaid, and is shape-coded in the legend (marker, colour, and line style). The exact method is correct up to 17 variables. Configurations using witnesses stay above $0.85$ up to roughly 60 variables and degrade gracefully thereafter; the witness-free configurations ($\mathrm  {wit\ off}$) underperform throughout, starting near $0.67$. Dynamic-set-size sampling ($\mathrm  {dyn\ on}$) is among the highest at moderate problem sizes.}}{51}{figure.caption.48}\protected@file@percent }
